            <div xml:id="d441">

                <pb facs="0499" n="391" xml:id="pg391"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.512/589: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-06-29T17:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 29, 1921—5
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received June 29—7:49
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>684. Following from American consul general at Shanghai: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“53. June 29, 11 a.m. Notice dated June 27 has just been issued by the
                            Surtax Revenue Department, Nanking, stating that the Nationalist
                            Government, Nanking, is proceeding to collect a surtax on exports
                            amounting to one-half of the existing customs export duty on and after
                            July 1, 1927. Notice specifying the rate of the surtax on luxuries will
                            be promulgated later. No action has been taken by any of the local
                            organizations.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
